{
  "about": "The level-box reads of a body that scripts/check_level_box_readers.py finds, each with its class. A new read is not in this file: convert it, or add it with the class that says why the level box is right there. A line the search no longer finds must be deleted: the counts may only fall. LEVEL-BOX-READERS in docs/planning/queue.md has the table.",
  "classes": {
    "DEFECT, a procedure written in world axes": "NOT a legitimate read: wrong in turned gravity. The ambush of a teleport puts 'behind' on world x and the feet on world y, and the petting mark is on world x at the petter's y. To turn this one half would give a wrong answer of another shape: state the procedure in the frame of the body (LEVEL-BOX-READERS, docs/planning/queue.md)",
    "to convert: portals": "a portal transit, an eviction and their draws read a body's level box; a body turns through a portal, so this class has its own frame questions",
    "to convert: what a brain sees of a peer": "the half extent a brain is given for a peer is level",
    "a shot": "a shot is a free body with no support and no stance: its size is its box",
    "the gravity of a body": "this box is what resolves the frame of the body, so the frame cannot turn it",
    "the centre only": "the reader takes the centre, which the two boxes share",
    "developer trace and overlay": "a developer tool, not the game; an overlay that draws the level box of a turned body shows a box the body does not have",
    "a game with no turned gravity": "Mary-O, Smash and Sanic have no room whose gravity is turned; convert when one does",
    "the camera's framing bounds": "a bound of what the camera frames, not a contact",
    "inside the kernel": "the kernel turns the half itself on this line, or the crawler arm states its own DOWN"
  },
